{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Add Feature Flags","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that owns a ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice, fetches a Swidux-defined JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a — same input always produces the same bucket, no network round-trip per read. Local overrides give QA a one-action toggle that wins over remote evaluation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","type":"reference"},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","text":"Before you start","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes you have a Swidux app already wired up — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You also need somewhere to host a JSON file. Any URL works — Cloudflare Pages, R2, S3, a Worker, your own backend. The plugin doesn’t care. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a runnable Cloudflare Worker that serves feature-flag ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" killswitch config for every app in a portfolio from one URL and one KV namespace, keyed ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/<appID>\/<resource>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — point this plugin at ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxFeatureFlags\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-2-Add-a-state-slice-and-action-case","text":"Step 2: Add a state slice and action case","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxFeatureFlags","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var featureFlags: FeatureFlagsState = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case featureFlags(FeatureFlagsAction)","    \/\/ ... your other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is needed in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" file that touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.featureFlags.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — including views that read flags for display. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"tip","name":"Tip","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Step-3-Hydrate-state-and-register-the-plugin","text":"Step 3: Hydrate state and register the plugin","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"At app launch, mint a stable per-install ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"device ID","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (Keychain-backed so it survives reinstall — this is the bucketing identity), hydrate state from your ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (so the last-known-good config survives cold launches), then register the plugin. Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"var deviceID: String = \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and point ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()                       \/\/ flags config cache","","\/\/ Stable bucketing identity — Keychain so it survives reinstall, and shared","\/\/ with analytics: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, …).","let deviceID = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.app\").deviceIdentity()","","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv, deviceID: deviceID),","    deviceID: deviceID",")","","let store = Store(initialState: initial, reducer: AppReducer())","","\/\/ With the Examples\/ConfigWorker setup this is the shared portfolio URL:","\/\/ \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\". Any URL returning FeatureFlagsConfig works.","let configURL = URL(static: \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\")","","let flags = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags,","    action: AppAction.featureFlags,","    extractAction: { if case .featureFlags(let a) = $0 { return a } else { return nil } },","    service: HTTPFeatureFlagsService(url: configURL),","    deviceIDKeyPath: \\.deviceID,","    keyValueStore: kv",")","store.register(plugin: flags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-4-Declare-typed-flag-keys","text":"Step 4: Declare typed flag keys","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare each flag once on a namespace so reads are type-safe:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension BoolFlag {","    static let newOnboarding = BoolFlag(\"new_onboarding\")","}","","enum CheckoutVariant: String { case control, treatment }","","extension VariantFlag where Variant == CheckoutVariant {","    static let checkoutLayout = VariantFlag(\"checkout_layout\", default: .control)","}","","extension ValueFlag where Value == Int {","    static let maxFreeUploads = ValueFlag(\"max_free_uploads\", default: 5)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-5-Read-flags-from-views","text":"Step 5: Read flags from views","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"code":["if store.featureFlags.isEnabled(.newOnboarding) {","    NewOnboardingView()","}","","let layout = store.featureFlags.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","let cap = store.featureFlags.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-6-Refresh-on-foreground","text":"Step 6: Refresh on foreground","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin debounces ","type":"text"},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the configured ","type":"text"},{"code":"RefreshPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it’s safe to dispatch on every ","type":"text"},{"code":"scenePhase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transition:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .active { store.send(.featureFlags(.refresh)) }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-7-Guard-against-forever-flags","text":"Step 7: Guard against forever flags","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Give every flag a required owner and expiry, and add one CI test that fails when a flag outlives its expiry. Declare a manifest alongside the typed keys — the factory ","type":"text"},{"code":"owner","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"expires","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameters are non-optional, and the keys are single-sourced from the flag declarations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum FlagManifest {","    static let all: [FlagDescriptor] = [","        .bool(.newOnboarding, owner: \"growth\",","              expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_788_000_000), purpose: \"New onboarding flow\"),","        .variant(.checkoutLayout, owner: \"checkout\",","                 expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_785_000_000), purpose: \"Checkout A\/B\"),","        .value(.maxFreeUploads, owner: \"platform\",","               expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_785_000_000), purpose: \"Free upload cap\"),","    ]","}","","@Test func noForeverFlags() {","    let report = FlagGovernance.expirationReport(FlagManifest.all)","    #expect(report == nil, \"\\(report ?? \"\")\")   \/\/ failure names each expired flag + owner","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a pure compile-time \/ test concern — no wire-format change and no effect on runtime evaluation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For wire format, bucketing, exposure tracking, and governance details, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentat